# Every text file in this repository is ultimately read inside a Linux
# container. Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, so a clone on
# Windows rewrites these files to CRLF on checkout - and the container's
# entrypoint then dies on a shebang that reads `bash\r`, with an error that
# names neither the file nor the cause:
#
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# The blobs were already stored with LF, so a Linux or macOS clone worked
# and a Windows clone did not. Pinning the working tree to LF makes the
# checkout identical on every platform instead of depending on whoever
# cloned it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Screenshots in evidence/ and the layout spacer the target app serves.
# `text=auto` already detects these, but declaring them makes the intent
# explicit rather than relying on heuristics.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
